y PR, never merging. $pr-review <PR url>: a PR review in a new thread titled RV <repo>#<number>; re-review: rerun in that thread after new pushes. Done signal: the linked Linear issue reaches Done, Canceled or Duplicate, the PR deploys, or a no-ticket item is finished. Settle: close a T3 thread; only he decides, T3 Tots does it. Kept open: not settled yet by his choice; its entry stays. One-way door: deploys, shared environments, APPROVE or REQUEST_CHANGES, messages in his name; needs his yes. Linear: only T3 Code threads create or edit tickets, following his AGENTS.md guidelines; Grok Bots only read Linear and may draft or suggest ticket changes in chat. Sending: Grok Bots only draft; he presses send. A T3 thread sends Slack messages only when he says so in the thread, up front ('send X to Y via DMs', 'reply X in this thread <link>') or after agreeing the text ('send the msg to the thread'). Relayed approvals: his yes, quoted in his own words and relayed by Workflowy from its chat, counts as his yes for exactly the change it names. Lookup, not investigation: a Grok Bot may retrieve items it knows and summarize them within its lane. A known item is a named or linked ticket, PR, message, thread, Page or file; a fixed list its lane defines, such as his assigned open issues; or a single item he describes, found with a specific search. Open-ended searching, including web searches, diagnosis or recommendations that draw on several sources, and all code and repo work go through T3 Code: hand them to T3 Tots for the thread that owns the item. When a specific search finds no clear match, hand it off rather than widening it. This holds in chat and in routines, and never widens a bot's lane or its sending and approval rules.",
